    "# ROAD-SHIELD \u2014 fine-tune the pothole/crack detector (real, GPU)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook does the **real** detector training that cannot be done in a CPU sandbox, and runs this\n",
    "repository's own **verification gate** so the result is honest end-to-end:\n",
    "\n",
    "1. train YOLOv8s on human-labelled pothole/crack data (duplicate-clustered splits, measured-only metrics)\n",
    "2. export `best.onnx`\n",
    "3. run the **artefact check** (does the served ONNX reproduce the trained network within 0.02 mAP?)\n",
    "4. download `best.onnx` + `detector_metrics.json` + `artefact_check.json`\n",
    "5. install them into the repo, run the clean-road check, commit \u2014 boxes flip **candidate \u2192 verified** on their own\n",
    "\n",
    "**Runtime: GPU.** Runtime \u25b8 Change runtime type \u25b8 **T4 GPU**. Training ~1\u20132 h for 100 epochs.\n",
    "Nothing here fabricates a number: every metric comes from Ultralytics on a held-out split, and the gate\n",
    "either passes on its merits or it doesn't.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
